{"type":"text","timestamp":1790375742783,"sessionID":"ses_f254fb702ffemytTpcdU1ARBLD","part":{"id":"prt_0dab5cd2c001oSJE3J2qivOf1B","messageID":"msg_0dab59e0d001csx2fmwalS3vh1","sessionID":"ses_f254fb702ffemytTpcdU1ARBLD","type":"text","text":"Implemented the security drone contact tracking setup.\n\n- Added the opposing-team group mapping in [unit_stats.gd](/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd).\n- Created [detect_range.gd](/workspace/custom_nodes/detect_range.gd) with the requested exports, collision layer/mask formulas, and circular range scaled by `attack_range`. The base range defaults to 32 pixels.\n- Created [target_finder.gd](/workspace/custom_nodes/target_finder.gd) with contact tracking, change signals, nearest opposing-unit selection, and `has_target_in_range()`.\n- Wired the nodes and exported references in [battle_unit.tscn](/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn), and added the onready references and stats assignment in [battle_unit.gd](/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd).\n\nValidated with Godot 4.4.1: the project loads successfully, and runtime checks passed for nearest-target selection, both teams’ detection settings, contact entry/exit, non-unit filtering, empty groups, and stats reassignment.\n\nThe [visual verification image](/workspace/target_tracking_verification.png) confirms the close intruder is inside the drone’s detection range and the distant intruder is outside it.","time":{"start":1790375742764,"end":1790375742768},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0ff8e04e201cc520016ab6f736397c87d19a987ce982036d68","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
